;; A yield point inside a body-local function, in an ordinary definition.
;;
;; The half of `errors/bjo_in_local_function.bjo` that survived. A local
;; function may suspend now — `158_local_functions.bjo` is the group of that —
;; but only where its *callers* can await it, and its callers are the enclosing
;; body. `outer` is a `defun`, so they cannot.
;;
;; Which means the reason has moved from the local function to the thing around
;; it, and the message had to move with it. Saying "a local function inside an
;; async method is not itself async" would now be false twice over: local
;; functions can be async, and there is no async method here anyway.
;;
;; The advice has to work, so it names the one change that fixes this: make
;; `outer` a bjoroutine. It deliberately does *not* offer `(defbjo (helper ...))`
;; — that is refused by the parser, and offering it would land the reader in a
;; second error, which is the one thing a diagnostic here may never do.
;;
;; `helper` is called twice on purpose. Called once, beta reduction would
;; substitute it away and the yield point would land in `outer`'s own body,
;; which is a different diagnostic.

;; EXPECT-ERROR: calling 'fetch' is a yield point
;; EXPECT-ERROR: yield point is not allowed here
;; EXPECT-ERROR: inside 'helper', a body-local function
;; EXPECT-ERROR: the definition around it is not a bjoroutine
;; EXPECT-ERROR: Make the enclosing definition a (defbjo ...)

(: fetch (-> int int))
(defbjo (fetch x) (* x 2))

(: outer (-> int int))
(defun (outer n)
  (defun (helper y) (fetch y))
  (+ (helper n) (helper (+ n 1))))

(defun (main args) 0)
